# Class Diagram — MRGym

The Class Diagram documents the software structure, class members, and relationships organized according to the Model-View-Controller (MVC) architectural pattern.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    direction TB

    namespace models {
        class User {
            -String _id
            -String email
            -String password
            -String name
            +User()
            +User(String, String, String)
            +getId() String
            +setId(String) void
            +getEmail() String
            +setEmail(String) void
            +getPassword() String
            +setPassword(String) void
            +getName() String
            +setName(String) void
            +toString() String
        }

        class Exercise {
            -int id
            -String name
            -String description
            +Exercise()
            +Exercise(int, String, String)
            +getId() int
            +setId(int) void
            +getName() String
            +setName(String) void
            +getDescription() String
            +setDescription(String) void
            +toString() String
        }

        class WorkoutPlan {
            -String _id
            -String name
            -List~Exercise~ exercises
            +WorkoutPlan()
            +WorkoutPlan(String, List~Exercise~)
            +getId() String
            +setId(String) void
            +getName() String
            +setName(String) void
            +getExercises() List~Exercise~
            +setExercises(List~Exercise~) void
            +toString() String
        }

        class WorkoutLog {
            -String _id
            -String userId
            -String date
            -int durationMinutes
            +WorkoutLog()
            +WorkoutLog(String, String, int)
            +getId() String
            +setId(String) void
            +getUserId() String
            +setUserId(String) void
            +getDate() String
            +setDate(String) void
            +getDurationMinutes() int
            +setDurationMinutes(int) void
            +toString() String
        }
    }

    namespace views {
        class CustomAdapter {
            -Context context
            -List~Exercise~ exerciseList
            +CustomAdapter(Context, List~Exercise~)
            +getCount() int
            +getItem(int) Object
            +getItemId(int) long
            +getView(int, View, ViewGroup) View
        }
    }

    namespace exceptions {
        class InvalidCredentialsException {
            +InvalidCredentialsException(String)
        }
    }

    namespace controllers {
        class LoginActivity {
            -EditText etEmail
            -EditText etPassword
            -Button btnLogin
            -Button btnGoToRegister
            #onCreate(Bundle) void
            -loginUser(String, String) void
        }

        class RegisterActivity {
            -EditText etName
            -EditText etEmail
            -EditText etPassword
            -Button btnRegister
            -Button btnGoToLogin
            #onCreate(Bundle) void
            -registerUser(String, String, String) void
        }

        class MainActivity {
            -Toolbar toolbar
            -ListView listViewExercises
            -CustomAdapter adapter
            -List~Exercise~ exerciseList
            -Button btnCamera
            -Button btnWorkout
            -Button btnProfile
            #onCreate(Bundle) void
            +onCreateOptionsMenu(Menu) boolean
            +onOptionsItemSelected(MenuItem) boolean
        }

        class WorkoutActivity {
            -Toolbar toolbar
            -ListView listViewWorkouts
            -TextView tvEmptyWorkouts
            -Button btnAddWorkout
            #onCreate(Bundle) void
            +onSupportNavigateUp() boolean
        }

        class ProfileActivity {
            -TextView tvUserEmail
            -Button btnLogoutProfile
            -Button btnBackProfile
            #onCreate(Bundle) void
        }

        class SharedPrefsUtils {
            -String PREF_NAME$
            -String KEY_EMAIL$
            -String KEY_TOKEN$
            +saveSession(Context, String, String)$ void
            +getEmail(Context)$ String
            +clearSession(Context)$ void
        }

        class RestClient {
            +makeRequest(String, String, String, String, VolleyCallback)$ void
        }
    }

    WorkoutPlan "1" o-- "*" Exercise : contains
    MainActivity --> CustomAdapter : uses
    CustomAdapter --> Exercise : displays
    LoginActivity ..> SharedPrefsUtils : reads/writes
    ProfileActivity ..> SharedPrefsUtils : reads/clears
    MainActivity ..> SharedPrefsUtils : clears
    LoginActivity ..> RestClient : invokes
    RegisterActivity ..> RestClient : invokes
    LoginActivity ..> InvalidCredentialsException : throws
```

## Architectural Overview

- **Models**: Plain Java domain classes (`User`, `Exercise`, `WorkoutPlan`, `WorkoutLog`) encapsulating business state and serialization without UI dependencies.
- **Views**: UI presentations using XML layouts and `CustomAdapter` (extending `BaseAdapter`) to render list rows.
- **Controllers**: Android Activities (`LoginActivity`, `RegisterActivity`, `MainActivity`, `WorkoutActivity`, `ProfileActivity`) coordinating UI interactions, plus service helpers (`RestClient` and `SharedPrefsUtils`).
- **Exceptions**: Custom business exception handling (`InvalidCredentialsException`) for authentication failures.
